From 6a4d9d6eeb30cda3d2d43da193ee0c0fcc913dc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Giuliani <lorenzo@frenzart.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:47:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] razermouse: add onboard button actions for the Naga LH 2020

The Naga Left-Handed Edition 2020 keeps its key bindings in onboard flash and
plays them back itself, so Windows Synapse is the only writer. The protocol is
class 02 command 0C for writes and 8C for reads, with the same
<type> <length> <data...> action encoding used by the Naga V2 Pro in #2962:
0x02 <mod> <usage> for a keyboard key, 0x0D <mod> <usage> <rate hi> <rate lo>
for autofire.

Add the button_action sysfs file for this device: writing three bytes selects
a button, writing "<store> <button> <layer> <action...>" stores the action and
sends the 00/B3 commit that makes it active without a replug. Reading returns
the ten-byte record.

The daemon side exposes razer.device.onboard with getButtons,
getButtonAction and setButtonAction on the existing device class.

Only the live profile (store 1) and the twelve thumb-grid controls
0x40..0x4B are exposed. Those are the combinations verified on hardware;
other controls use a different input class and are left alone.

The read request carries the input class in argument 3 (0x02 for the thumb
grid); without it this firmware does not answer mapping reads.
